    <!-- SECTION 3 -->
    <section class="section" id="s3">
      <h2>3. Network Forensics — Overview</h2>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p>
        Network forensics is the monitoring, capture, storage, and analysis of network traffic for the purposes of
        intrusion detection, incident response, and legal evidence collection. If memory forensics is like examining a
        suspect's brain, network forensics is like reviewing the CCTV footage of every conversation they had.
      </p>
      <p>
        Network forensics operates at two levels: <strong>catch-it-as-you-can</strong> (live capture of all traffic in
        real time) and <strong>stop-look-and-listen</strong> (analysis of pre-captured packet data). Both approaches
        have distinct use cases in enterprise security.
      </p>

