        <li><strong>Timestamp alignment:</strong> Match time of suspicious PCAP traffic with process creation times in
          memory</li>
        <li><strong>Payload ↔ Memory:</strong> C2 shellcode payload found in PCAP and the same code pattern found in
          process memory via malfind</li>
        <li><strong>DNS ↔ Connection:</strong> DNS query in PCAP resolves to IP, then that IP appears in memory netstat
        </li>
        <li><strong>Credentials:</strong> Captured HTTP form POST (cleartext creds in PCAP) correlates with new admin
          account creation seen in registry hive from memory</li>
      </ul>
